  "notes": "Calls Bio.SeqUtils.MeltingTemp.Tm_NN 48k times on seeded random ACGT sequences (15-60 nt) across saltcorr 0-7 and varied salt concentrations, using str, lowercase str and Seq inputs. On head this goes through the new C extension _meltingtemp_exact. Every tenth call passes a float saltcorr, which the C function rejects, so head runs the new fallback-to-Python branch. Head coverage is 12/14 changed lines; the missed lines are the ImportError branch, which can't run while the extension is present. Outputs are equal (rounded to 6 decimals). Base 3.0 s, head 1.2 s. The C code segfaults on sequences over 10,000 nt and on '' passed directly to the C function, and gives a different Tm than Python for sequences containing N; the workload avoids these inputs."
